  "body": "The fixed-model geometry-scoring experiment passed all 25 prespecified checks. Reusing all six trained models, geometry reduced persistent-GRU native control cost by 35.7% on six-step sensing gaps and 28.7% on ten-step gaps. With both families using geometry, GRU cost was 22.6% and 15.7% lower than cached MLP, improving every paired fit.\n\nGeometry added about 53% to measured GRU whole-controller time. This is a successful scoring intervention, not a new architecture, biological advantage or matched-total-compute claim. Full-sensing GRU also improved 36.4%, so the gain is not specific to observation gaps. The earlier cache study remains failed at 15/28 checks.\n\n[Results and limits](https://github.com/kw2828/OpenJev/blob/39b0c929bf6292fa9aa7f1934526a53d6ffd93d1/research/reacher-geometry-score.md) include every fit, all 51 control rows, compute measurements, the first scheduled schematic replay and an independent interpretation review.\n\nThe saved-output audit replayed 329,088 native transitions with zero discrepancy, checked all 80 frozen source files and unchanged before/after model tensors, and reconstructed search decisions without new learned-model calls. Neural predictions remain saved source-bound evidence. Physics references use one 64-candidate bank and a different nominal objective; learned controllers use CEM256. Exposed-root diagnostics and three inherited fit pairs do not establish broad generalization.\n\nAssets preserve the complete scientific execution, six inherited checkpoints, audit, figures and replay. The separate engineering archive includes both unsuccessful and successful preparation attempts and their original receipts. No new fitting or Astra calls occurred in this study.\n\nUse the attached README, receipt, manifest and SHA256SUMS to verify and reconstruct split archives. Concatenate each archive's parts in the order specified by its receipt before extraction. Older upstream lineage releases remain separate dependencies. The package receipt records local verification before upload; the repository's later publication receipt records remote asset verification.\n\nThe next proposed experiment compares persistent, current-only and cached-observation GRUs under the same geometry score. It is not part of these completed results.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-19T02:26:05Z",
